description:
FILED s539a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-13) -- the CAUSE of #3619.

Reproducer (scratch/s539a/pr/cz3.pl in the s539a worktree; needs IO-Compress-2.214-0/lib on @INC):
  use Test::More tests => 1;
  BEGIN { use_ok('IO::Compress::Gzip::Constants'); }
  my $n = 0;
  for my $index ( GZIP_MIN_HEADER_SIZE + 1 .. GZIP_MIN_HEADER_SIZE + GZIP_FEXTRA_HEADER_SIZE + 1) { $n++ }
  print "# extra loop count: $n\n";
perl: 3 (and 4 for the Name loop); PCL (main 24988e35): 1 and 1.  The same constants imported by `BEGIN { require X; X->import }` (pr/cz4.pl) are right on main: the static parse sees that spelling as a `use`, but not a `use_ok` call.  So each of cz-03zlib-v1.t's four header-truncation loops (Extra 3, Name 4, Comment 7, CRC 2 iterations in perl) runs ONCE: 12 x 6 = 72 rows never emitted, the file ends cleanly at 400 of 472.  146 test files under ~/.cpan/build use the `BEGIN { use_ok(...) }` shape.

RULED by the reviewing session (s541, rule 9a): the fact `a call of this sub imports from the module named by its first argument` is DATA declared with the sub (lib/Test/More.pm or a lib/PCL/Facts/ overlay, a marker on its forward declaration); the MECHANISM in Pl/ is keyed on the marker, never a name: a call, as a statement directly in a BEGIN block's body, of a sub carrying the marker, with a literal module name first, is treated FOR PARSE FACTS ONLY as `use MODULE LIST` at that position.  Outside BEGIN: no effect.  Non-literal first argument: no effect, no die.

The #2610 detector LOGS these sites but stays silent in announce mode: #4882.
